Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: apps/dgst.c
Line: 452
Function: dgst_main
Bug type: null-pointer-dereference
CWE: CWE-476
Explanation: When -xoflen is specified and a oneshot signing key is used (e.g., Ed25519/Ed448 where the default digest is UNDEF), md can remain NULL. The code then calls EVP_MD_xof(md) before rejecting signing with XOF, dereferencing a NULL md and causing a crash. Concrete path: use -sign with an Ed25519 key and -xoflen > 0; oneshot_sign==1 skips md initialization, leading to md==NULL at this call.

